WEBVTT

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:05.543
Domino's.

00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:08.165
Level 1.

00:00:08.225 --> 00:00:09.767
Pollyanna.

00:00:09.827 --> 00:00:10.668
By Eleanor H.

00:00:10.688 --> 00:00:12.920
Porter.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.882
Chapter 1.

00:00:14.942 --> 00:00:16.912
Miss Polly.

00:00:16.972 --> 00:00:22.708
Miss Polly Harrington came quickly into her kitchen that June morning.

00:00:22.768 --> 00:00:28.653
Nancy, please stop your work for a minute and listen to me, she said.

00:00:28.713 --> 00:00:31.169
Nancy stopped at once.

00:00:31.229 --> 00:00:34.414
Miss Polly wasn't easy to please.

00:00:34.474 --> 00:00:38.477
Usually she wanted Nancy to work more quickly.

00:00:38.537 --> 00:00:52.716
Nancy's father was dead, her mother was ill, and she had two younger sisters and a brother at home, so she came to work for Miss Harrington, one of the richest women in town.

00:00:52.776 --> 00:01:00.768
But Miss Polly was always angry when she did things badly, and never smiled when she did them right.

00:01:00.828 --> 00:01:08.221
Later today, said Miss Polly, you can make the little back attic ready for a visitor.

00:01:08.281 --> 00:01:13.276
My niece, Miss Pollyanna Whittier, is coming to stay.

00:01:13.336 --> 00:01:15.628
She's 11 years old.

00:01:15.688 --> 00:01:17.859
Is a little girl coming here?

00:01:17.879 --> 00:01:19.591
That's nice.

00:01:19.651 --> 00:01:21.272
Cried Nancy.

00:01:21.332 --> 00:01:25.513
She thought of her two happy little sisters at home.

00:01:25.573 --> 00:01:28.874
Nice, said Miss Polly coldly.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:31.405
I don't know about that.

00:01:31.465 --> 00:01:35.536
Nancy's face was suddenly hot and red.

00:01:35.596 --> 00:01:39.357
But she's your sister's child, Miss.

00:01:39.417 --> 00:01:42.028
Of course you want her here.

00:01:42.088 --> 00:01:49.862
Nancy, my silly sister married young, had children early, and couldn't care for them.

00:01:49.922 --> 00:01:54.364
I don't want to care for this child, but I must.

00:01:54.424 --> 00:01:57.035
Now don't forget that attic.

00:01:57.095 --> 00:02:00.577
And with that, she left the kitchen.

00:02:00.637 --> 00:02:09.904
Back in her room, Miss Polly opened the letter from a far away town in the West, and read it again.

00:02:09.964 --> 00:02:15.659
Ms. Harrington, I have sad news for you.

00:02:15.719 --> 00:02:21.151
Your sister's husband, John Whittier, died two weeks ago.

00:02:21.211 --> 00:02:25.783
He leaves a girl 11 years old behind him.

00:02:25.843 --> 00:02:31.245
John was the minister in the church here and wasn't very rich.

00:02:31.305 --> 00:02:35.227
His child has nobody to care for her now.

00:02:35.286 --> 00:02:42.463
Only you, her family in the east, John spoke of this before he died.

00:02:42.523 --> 00:02:44.634
Can you take her?

00:02:44.694 --> 00:02:48.696
We can put Pollyanna on the train to come to you.

00:02:48.756 --> 00:02:57.752
When I get your answer, and please say yes, I can write and tell you the day and time of the train.

00:02:57.812 --> 00:03:03.088
Jeremiah O White.

00:03:03.147 --> 00:03:12.564
Miss Polly sat with the letter in her hand and thought of her sister Jenny, the girl's mother.

00:03:12.624 --> 00:03:22.561
When Jenny was 20, a rich older man from the town wanted to marry her, but she wasn't interested in him or his money.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:26.593
She wanted to marry young John Whittier for love.

00:03:26.653 --> 00:03:31.094
Her parents weren't happy about it, but she didn't listen to them.

00:03:31.154 --> 00:03:36.536
She married, left home, and went west with her new husband.

00:03:36.596 --> 00:03:39.216
Miss Polly remembered it well.

00:03:39.276 --> 00:03:43.697
She was only fifteen, the youngest at the time.

00:03:43.757 --> 00:03:47.424
Her parents wanted nothing more to do with Jenny.

00:03:47.484 --> 00:03:50.411
Of course, Jenny wrote for a time.

00:03:50.471 --> 00:03:56.965
Her letters told them about her different children, but they all died when they were very young.

00:03:57.024 --> 00:04:00.277
Only the last child lived.

00:04:00.337 --> 00:04:07.219
Jenny gave her the name Pollyanna after her two sisters, Polly and Anna.

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:10.610
That was their last news from her.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:16.264
Some years later, a letter came for them from a small town in the West.

00:04:16.324 --> 00:04:20.749
It was from John Whittier and brought sad news.

00:04:20.808 --> 00:04:23.050
Jenny was dead.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:27.104
Miss Polly thought about the past 25 years.

00:04:27.164 --> 00:04:29.496
She was 40 years old.

00:04:29.556 --> 00:04:33.576
Her father, mother, and sisters were all dead.

00:04:33.636 --> 00:04:39.738
The big family house and all her father's money were now in her name.

00:04:39.798 --> 00:04:44.061
Some people said to her, why don't you live with a friend?

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.982
But she didn't want a friend in the house.

00:04:47.042 --> 00:04:49.275
She liked living quietly.

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:52.968
And now, Miss Polly stood up.

00:04:53.028 --> 00:04:58.602
She was happy, of course, to do the right thing and to take the girl into her home.

00:04:58.662 --> 00:05:05.262
But Polly Anna, what a silly name.

00:05:05.322 --> 00:05:11.742
Later that morning, Nancy made the back attic ready.

00:05:11.802 --> 00:05:19.034
Why is she putting the child here when she has lots of nicer rooms in the house to give her?

00:05:19.094 --> 00:05:21.165
She thought.

00:05:21.224 --> 00:05:27.186
That afternoon, she went out into the garden to speak to old Tom.

00:05:27.246 --> 00:05:29.807
He worked for Miss Polly there.

00:05:29.867 --> 00:05:35.766
Mr. Tom, a little girl's coming to live here, she said.

00:05:35.826 --> 00:05:37.703
Not with Miss Polly.

00:05:37.723 --> 00:05:39.904
Left, Tom.

00:05:39.964 --> 00:05:45.538
Yes, she told me earlier today, answered Nancy.

00:05:45.597 --> 00:05:47.439
It's her niece.

00:05:47.498 --> 00:05:49.860
She's 11 years old.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.742
That's Miss Jenny's little girl then.

00:05:52.802 --> 00:05:54.593
The old man said.

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:56.854
And now she's coming to stay.

00:05:56.874 --> 00:05:58.994
That's wonderful.

00:05:59.054 --> 00:06:03.596
She's going to sleep in the attic, said Nancy.

00:06:03.656 --> 00:06:07.350
For me, that's not right.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:13.154
Old Tom didn't look happy at this, but then he gave a big smile.

00:06:13.214 --> 00:06:17.758
Say, what's Miss Polly going to do with a child in the house?

00:06:17.818 --> 00:06:20.810
He said, more important.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:26.674
What's a child going to do with Miss Polly in the house, answered Nancy?

00:06:26.734 --> 00:06:29.382
The old man laughed.

00:06:29.442 --> 00:06:33.919
You don't like Miss Polly, he said.

00:06:33.979 --> 00:06:37.249
Nobody does, answered Nancy.

00:06:37.269 --> 00:06:42.240
Ah, but you didn't know her when she was in love.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:45.391
In love, cried Nancy.

00:06:45.451 --> 00:06:48.821
Nobody loved her back, of course.

00:06:48.881 --> 00:06:52.522
Oh, yes they did, said old Tom.

00:06:52.582 --> 00:06:55.793
And the man's living here in the town today.

00:06:55.813 --> 00:06:57.483
Who is he?

00:06:57.543 --> 00:07:00.074
It's not right to tell you.

00:07:00.134 --> 00:07:03.755
He said, and he looked up at the house.

00:07:03.815 --> 00:07:07.396
He was a true friend to the Harrington family.

00:07:07.456 --> 00:07:10.907
You could see it in his old blue eyes.

00:07:10.967 --> 00:07:14.278
So Miss Polly had a lover.

00:07:14.298 --> 00:07:18.499
I can't believe it, said Nancy.

00:07:18.559 --> 00:07:23.661
Well, when she was younger, she was beautiful.

00:07:23.721 --> 00:07:26.012
And she can be again.

00:07:26.072 --> 00:07:27.716
Said old Tom.

00:07:27.776 --> 00:07:29.310
Beautiful!

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:30.982
Miss Polly!

00:07:31.042 --> 00:07:32.153
Yes.

00:07:32.212 --> 00:07:41.278
She needs to wear hats with flowers on them, to have her hair different, and to wear nice dresses again.

00:07:41.338 --> 00:07:44.820
Miss Polly's not old, Nancy.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:49.592
Well, she's never happy, said Nancy.

00:07:49.652 --> 00:07:53.114
And one of these days I'm going to leave.

00:07:53.174 --> 00:07:55.527
Goodbye, Nancy.

00:07:55.587 --> 00:07:58.812
It's not easy for you, I know.

00:07:58.872 --> 00:08:00.554
Said old Tom.

00:08:00.614 --> 00:08:02.867
But don't leave.

00:08:02.927 --> 00:08:06.311
And with that, he went back to his work.

00:08:06.371 --> 00:08:10.436
Nancy called a cold voice from the house.

00:08:10.496 --> 00:08:16.934
Yes, Miss, cried Nancy, and she ran in at once.

00:08:16.994 --> 00:08:25.850
Some days later, Miss Polly told Nancy, my niece is arriving by train tomorrow at four.

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:29.122
You can go with Timothy in the buggy and meet her.

00:08:29.182 --> 00:08:34.246
The letter says, fair hair, red dress, and a summer hat.

00:08:34.305 --> 00:08:37.788
You can find her with that, I'm sure.

00:08:37.848 --> 00:08:45.588
The next afternoon, Nancy and Timothy, old Tom's son, went to meet the train.

00:08:45.648 --> 00:08:49.616
Is she a good, quiet child, do you think?

00:08:49.676 --> 00:08:51.147
Ask Nancy.

00:08:51.207 --> 00:08:52.387
Who knows?

00:08:52.448 --> 00:08:54.049
Smile, Timothy.

00:08:54.109 --> 00:09:00.624
But a bad, noisy child isn't going to make things easy at the house for any of us.

00:09:00.684 --> 00:09:02.686
You can be sure of that.

00:09:02.746 --> 00:09:11.022
When the train arrived, a little girl with long, fair hair, a red dress, and a summer hat got off.

00:09:11.082 --> 00:09:16.556
It was Pollyanna.

00:09:16.616 --> 00:09:32.812
Chapter two the glad game Soon Pollyanna was in the buggy between Timothy and Nancy and they were on the road to miss Polly's house.

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:44.475
I Didn't have a black dress to wear said Pollyanna, but it's easier to be glad in red than black I guess Glad cried Nancy.

00:09:44.535 --> 00:09:49.962
Yes Because now father's with mother and my dead brothers and sisters.

00:09:50.022 --> 00:09:52.643
Father said that before he died.

00:09:52.703 --> 00:09:55.374
And of course I'm glad too.

00:09:55.434 --> 00:09:58.266
Because I have you Aunt Polly.

00:09:58.326 --> 00:09:59.536
Me?

00:09:59.596 --> 00:10:02.008
But I'm Nancy.

00:10:02.068 --> 00:10:04.319
I work for Miss Polly.

00:10:04.379 --> 00:10:06.680
Oh, I see.

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.632
Answered Pollyanna.

00:10:08.692 --> 00:10:12.214
So, she didn't come to meet me.

00:10:12.274 --> 00:10:15.534
Well, I'm glad about that.

00:10:15.594 --> 00:10:20.834
Because now I have you, and I'm going to meet her soon too.

00:10:20.894 --> 00:10:24.686
Miss Polly was in the front room when they arrived.

00:10:24.746 --> 00:10:26.506
Hello, Pollyanna.

00:10:26.566 --> 00:10:29.037
She said without a smile.

00:10:29.097 --> 00:10:33.728
Pollyanna ran and took the older woman in her arms.

00:10:33.788 --> 00:10:37.189
I'm very glad to meet you Aunt Polly.

00:10:37.249 --> 00:10:40.426
Now, about my red dress.

00:10:40.486 --> 00:10:41.753
Father said.

00:10:41.813 --> 00:10:44.666
Let's not talk about your father, child.

00:10:44.726 --> 00:10:45.666
Your bag.

00:10:45.726 --> 00:10:47.488
There isn't much in it.

00:10:47.548 --> 00:10:50.401
Only Father's books and Pollyanna.

00:10:50.461 --> 00:10:53.014
I don't want to hear about your father.

00:10:53.074 --> 00:10:54.315
Do you understand?

00:10:54.375 --> 00:10:56.166
Yes, Aunt Polly.

00:10:56.226 --> 00:10:58.118
Said the girl, sadly.

00:10:58.178 --> 00:11:00.170
Your bag's in your room.

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:01.932
Aunt Polly finished.

00:11:01.992 --> 00:11:03.484
Timothy took it up.

00:11:03.544 --> 00:11:05.054
So come with me.

00:11:05.114 --> 00:11:08.818
Pollyanna went upstairs after her aunt.

00:11:08.878 --> 00:11:17.998
There were lots of beautiful pictures to left and right, wonderful rooms, and a nice green carpet under her feet.

00:11:18.058 --> 00:11:23.422
But when they went into her room, it had no pictures or carpet in it.

00:11:23.482 --> 00:11:25.905
Only a bed, a chair.

00:11:25.965 --> 00:11:29.598
A window, a table, and a closet.

00:11:29.658 --> 00:11:32.410
Here we are, said Miss Polly.

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:34.961
Nancy can help you put your things away.

00:11:35.021 --> 00:11:36.862
Supper's at six o'clock.

00:11:36.922 --> 00:11:40.454
And with that, she went downstairs.

00:11:40.514 --> 00:11:46.398
When Nancy came up, she found Pollyanna with her hands over her face.

00:11:46.458 --> 00:11:54.242
Sadly, the girl opened her bag, and Nancy took some old dresses and books from it and put them away.

00:11:54.302 --> 00:11:58.374
At the same time, Pollyanna looked through the window.

00:11:58.434 --> 00:12:06.698
Oh, Nancy, I don't need pictures when I can see houses, trees, and the river through this, she said.

00:12:06.758 --> 00:12:10.843
Just then, they heard a bell downstairs.

00:12:10.903 --> 00:12:17.090
I must go now," said Nancy, and she went down to help with the supper.

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:22.794
Pollyanna soon felt hot in her room, and she opened the window.

00:12:22.854 --> 00:12:30.810
Then, with a laugh, she climbed out through the window, down the tree in front of it, and into the garden.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:35.324
From there, she ran to a little hill not far away.

00:12:35.384 --> 00:12:39.372
Old Tom was in the garden, and he saw her go.

00:12:39.432 --> 00:12:45.399
Soon she was up the hill and she didn't hear the supper bell at six o'clock.

00:12:45.459 --> 00:12:51.321
My niece is late, said Miss Polly to Nancy at the supper table.

00:12:51.381 --> 00:12:54.572
She can have bread and milk in the kitchen.

00:12:54.632 --> 00:13:00.154
After supper, Nancy went upstairs, but Pollyanna wasn't in her room.

00:13:00.214 --> 00:13:02.985
So Nancy went out into the garden.

00:13:03.045 --> 00:13:05.694
Pollyanna's up the hill over there.

00:13:05.754 --> 00:13:07.414
said old Tom.

00:13:07.474 --> 00:13:11.096
Nancy went at once and brought the girl in.

00:13:11.156 --> 00:13:13.196
How did you get out there?

00:13:13.256 --> 00:13:14.788
Nancy asked.

00:13:14.848 --> 00:13:17.118
Pollyanna told her.

00:13:17.178 --> 00:13:20.380
Well, you were late for supper.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:25.852
So you must have bread and milk with me in the kitchen tonight, your aunt says.

00:13:25.912 --> 00:13:28.304
Oh, I'm glad.

00:13:28.364 --> 00:13:29.954
Smiled Pollyanna.

00:13:30.014 --> 00:13:31.896
I like bread and milk.

00:13:31.956 --> 00:13:35.328
And I'd like to have supper with you too.

00:13:35.388 --> 00:13:39.300
How can you be glad about everything?

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:42.711
Well, it's the glad game, you know.

00:13:42.771 --> 00:13:44.592
My father taught it to me.

00:13:44.652 --> 00:13:48.473
You must always find the good in everything and be glad about it.

00:13:48.533 --> 00:13:50.454
It isn't always easy.

00:13:50.514 --> 00:13:54.235
Before bed, Miss Polly spoke to her niece.

00:13:54.295 --> 00:14:00.488
I'm sorry about supper tonight, Pollyanna, but you must learn to be on time.

00:14:00.548 --> 00:14:03.589
Oh, don't feel bad, Aunt Polly.

00:14:03.648 --> 00:14:05.044
Said Pollyanna.

00:14:05.104 --> 00:14:09.640
I was glad to have bread and milk in the kitchen with Nancy.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:15.002
The next afternoon, Miss Polly took Pollyanna into town.

00:14:15.062 --> 00:14:18.783
We must get you some new clothes, she said.

00:14:18.843 --> 00:14:20.163
New clothes?

00:14:20.223 --> 00:14:21.544
Cried Pollyanna.

00:14:21.604 --> 00:14:23.254
You're very good to me.

00:14:23.274 --> 00:14:27.455
I don't know about good, answered Miss Polly.

00:14:27.515 --> 00:14:31.557
With you and old clothes, people are going to think badly of me.

00:14:31.577 --> 00:14:33.356
I don't want that.

00:14:33.416 --> 00:14:36.188
Of course not, said Pollyanna.

00:14:36.248 --> 00:14:38.640
And you are good, Aunt Polly.

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:41.434
But you don't feel glad about it.

00:14:41.494 --> 00:14:42.894
Why not?

00:14:42.954 --> 00:14:46.178
I'm always glad when I do something good.

00:14:46.238 --> 00:14:48.150
Be quiet, child.

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:49.602
Said Miss Polly.

00:14:49.662 --> 00:14:51.854
Or we're going home this minute.

00:14:51.914 --> 00:14:55.486
Pollyanna stopped talking at once.

00:14:55.546 --> 00:15:02.285
That evening it was very hot again in Pollyanna's room, and she couldn't sleep.

00:15:02.345 --> 00:15:06.746
So she got out of bed and went to the back attic room.

00:15:06.806 --> 00:15:12.687
She opened the window there and climbed out onto the roof of Miss Polly's room.

00:15:12.747 --> 00:15:15.517
I can sleep here, she thought.

00:15:15.577 --> 00:15:21.148
But Miss Polly heard noises in the night and called Timothy on the telephone.

00:15:21.208 --> 00:15:24.219
Come quickly, there's someone on my roof.

00:15:24.279 --> 00:15:25.616
She cried.

00:15:25.676 --> 00:15:31.272
When Timothy came, he found Pollyanna out on the roof and took her in.

00:15:31.332 --> 00:15:34.398
What were you doing on my roof, girl?

00:15:34.458 --> 00:15:36.191
asked Miss Polly angrily.

00:15:36.211 --> 00:15:38.448
Oh, and Polly?

00:15:38.508 --> 00:15:41.884
I wanted to sleep out under the night sky.

00:15:41.944 --> 00:15:43.494
Began, Pollyanna.

00:15:43.554 --> 00:15:50.727
Well, now you must sleep in bed with me tonight, Pollyanna, because I don't want this to happen again.

00:15:50.747 --> 00:15:52.518
Oh, thank you.

00:15:52.578 --> 00:15:54.028
Cried Pollyanna.

00:15:54.088 --> 00:15:57.719
What a wonderful thing to sleep in my aunt's bed.

00:15:57.779 --> 00:15:59.950
Miss Polly couldn't speak.

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:08.401
Why, when she wanted to punish her niece, was the girl always glad.

00:16:08.461 --> 00:16:21.033
Chapter 3 New Friends The weeks went by, and Pollyanna felt happy in her new home.

00:16:21.093 --> 00:16:24.674
But it wasn't easy to talk to Miss Polly.

00:16:24.734 --> 00:16:30.466
Nancy was Pollyanna's only friend, and she always had work to do.

00:16:30.526 --> 00:16:34.480
So Pollyanna wanted to go out and meet people.

00:16:34.541 --> 00:16:37.974
Mrs. Snow lived not far away.

00:16:38.034 --> 00:16:42.565
She was a very sick woman and never left her bed.

00:16:42.625 --> 00:16:49.376
Miss Polly usually sent Nancy to her house on Thursday afternoons with something for her to eat.

00:16:49.436 --> 00:16:52.187
Chicken, soup, or jelly.

00:16:52.247 --> 00:16:53.937
Can I go today?

00:16:53.997 --> 00:16:57.238
Pollyanna asked Nancy one Thursday.

00:16:57.298 --> 00:17:01.438
Mrs. Snow's never happy, said Nancy.

00:17:01.498 --> 00:17:04.707
When she gets chicken, she wants soup.

00:17:04.767 --> 00:17:07.896
When it's soup, she wants jelly.

00:17:07.956 --> 00:17:10.148
You don't want to go.

00:17:10.208 --> 00:17:11.758
Yes, I do.

00:17:11.819 --> 00:17:16.271
So Pollyanna went to Mrs. Snow's house that afternoon.

00:17:16.331 --> 00:17:24.135
Miss Snow, a tired young woman, took the girl to her mother and left her there in the dark room.

00:17:24.195 --> 00:17:26.746
Here's some jelly from Aunt Polly.

00:17:26.806 --> 00:17:28.493
Said Pollyanna.

00:17:28.553 --> 00:17:33.682
I wanted soup today, said Mrs. Snow from the bed.

00:17:33.742 --> 00:17:37.125
That's strange, cried Pollyanna.

00:17:37.186 --> 00:17:43.110
Usually, you want chicken when you get jelly and soup when it's chicken.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.982
Nancy told me.

00:17:45.042 --> 00:17:47.403
Mrs. Snow sat up.

00:17:47.463 --> 00:17:50.996
What a thing to say, she cried.

00:17:51.056 --> 00:17:52.687
Who are you?

00:17:52.707 --> 00:17:55.358
I'm Miss Polly's niece.

00:17:55.418 --> 00:17:57.096
I live with her now.

00:17:57.156 --> 00:17:59.564
And I'm here with your jelly.

00:17:59.624 --> 00:18:01.565
I'm not hungry.

00:18:01.625 --> 00:18:06.858
I didn't sleep at all last night, said Mrs. Snow.

00:18:06.918 --> 00:18:10.491
That's wonderful, said Pollyanna.

00:18:10.551 --> 00:18:13.784
We lose lots of time when we sleep.

00:18:13.844 --> 00:18:16.876
I'd like not to sleep at night too.

00:18:16.936 --> 00:18:18.837
What's that?

00:18:18.897 --> 00:18:20.958
Open the curtains.

00:18:21.018 --> 00:18:23.216
I want to see you.

00:18:23.276 --> 00:18:25.252
said Mrs. Snow.

00:18:25.312 --> 00:18:28.443
So Pollyanna opened the curtains.

00:18:28.503 --> 00:18:30.303
You're beautiful!

00:18:30.363 --> 00:18:34.424
cried Pollyanna when she saw Mrs. Snow in the sun.

00:18:34.484 --> 00:18:37.884
I love your dark eyes and hair.

00:18:37.944 --> 00:18:45.146
That afternoon Pollyanna did Mrs. Snow's hair and put a pink flower in it.

00:18:45.206 --> 00:18:50.697
Miss Snow had a surprise when she came in after Pollyanna left.

00:18:50.757 --> 00:18:52.182
Mother!

00:18:52.242 --> 00:18:55.400
The curtains, she cried.

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:59.586
I wanted them open, said Mrs. Snow.

00:18:59.646 --> 00:19:03.882
And why do people bring me only things to eat?

00:19:03.942 --> 00:19:08.906
I'd like something nice to wear sometimes too.

00:19:08.966 --> 00:19:15.650
In September, after a long summer, Pollyanna started school.

00:19:15.711 --> 00:19:19.584
On her first morning, she met a man in the street.

00:19:19.644 --> 00:19:26.751
He wore a tall black hat and a long black coat, and he didn't smile.

00:19:26.812 --> 00:19:28.734
It's a nice day!

00:19:28.794 --> 00:19:30.404
Said Pollyanna.

00:19:30.464 --> 00:19:32.156
Are you talking to me?

00:19:32.216 --> 00:19:33.950
He said angrily.

00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:35.802
He didn't stop.

00:19:35.862 --> 00:19:40.483
The next day, when Pollyanna saw him, he had an umbrella.

00:19:40.543 --> 00:19:44.034
I don't like it when it rains, she said.

00:19:44.094 --> 00:19:46.524
But it doesn't rain every day.

00:19:46.584 --> 00:19:48.485
I'm glad about that.

00:19:48.545 --> 00:19:51.155
The man said nothing.

00:19:51.215 --> 00:19:53.076
Did he hear me?

00:19:53.136 --> 00:19:54.546
She thought.

00:19:54.606 --> 00:19:59.777
The day after, when they next met, the sun was in the sky.

00:19:59.837 --> 00:20:04.583
Pollyanna said, It's a nicer day than yesterday.

00:20:04.643 --> 00:20:06.114
Who are you?

00:20:06.174 --> 00:20:07.964
Said the man angrily.

00:20:08.024 --> 00:20:11.026
And why do you always tell me about the weather?

00:20:11.086 --> 00:20:14.016
I have more important things to think about.

00:20:14.077 --> 00:20:18.568
I'm telling you, because you don't have time to look at the sky.

00:20:18.628 --> 00:20:20.629
I'm Pollyanna Whittier.

00:20:20.689 --> 00:20:21.960
Who are you?

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:23.410
Why of all the...

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:24.881
began the man.

00:20:24.941 --> 00:20:26.411
Then he walked away.

00:20:26.431 --> 00:20:32.679
The next time Pollyanna met him, he said, Good afternoon.

00:20:32.739 --> 00:20:35.671
And before you speak, can I say something?

00:20:35.731 --> 00:20:38.444
It's a beautiful day, and I know it.

00:20:38.504 --> 00:20:39.484
Yes.

00:20:39.544 --> 00:20:43.858
I saw it in your smile before you spoke, said Pollyanna.

00:20:43.918 --> 00:20:45.029
Did you?

00:20:45.088 --> 00:20:47.080
answered the man.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:54.536
Nancy had a surprise when she went for a walk with Pollyanna, and the man said, Good afternoon.

00:20:54.596 --> 00:20:55.896
To them.

00:20:55.956 --> 00:20:59.760
He spoke to you, Nancy cried.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:00.711
Yes.

00:21:00.771 --> 00:21:04.834
He always does, now, answered Pollyanna.

00:21:04.894 --> 00:21:08.466
But that's John Pendleton.

00:21:08.526 --> 00:21:12.329
He lives alone in a house on Pendleton Hill.

00:21:12.389 --> 00:21:15.211
He never speaks to people.

00:21:15.271 --> 00:21:22.155
My friend Sally works at the hotel in town, and he never talks when he eats there.

00:21:22.215 --> 00:21:26.018
He never eats expensively, of course.

00:21:26.078 --> 00:21:30.276
It isn't easy without money, said Pollyanna.

00:21:30.336 --> 00:21:35.064
He's the richest man in town, answered Nancy.

00:21:35.125 --> 00:21:38.498
But he doesn't like giving his money away.

00:21:38.558 --> 00:21:40.749
He's strange.

00:21:40.809 --> 00:21:44.022
Maybe he's strange when you don't know him.

00:21:44.082 --> 00:21:45.763
Said Pollyanna.

00:21:45.823 --> 00:21:48.114
But I like him.

00:21:48.174 --> 00:21:54.620
At about that time, Pollyanna found a little cat in the street and took it home.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:58.836
After that she found a little dog and took that home too.

00:21:58.896 --> 00:22:05.690
Miss Polly didn't like animals, but it wasn't easy to say no to Pollyanna.

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:10.602
So fluffy the cat and Buffy the Dog stayed.

00:22:10.662 --> 00:22:16.924
October came, and one day Pollyanna met a boy in the street near her house.

00:22:16.984 --> 00:22:19.885
He was thin and in old clothes.

00:22:19.946 --> 00:22:21.136
Who are you?

00:22:21.196 --> 00:22:22.776
asked Pollyanna.

00:22:22.836 --> 00:22:25.178
And what are you doing here?

00:22:25.238 --> 00:22:27.000
I'm Jimmy Bean.

00:22:27.060 --> 00:22:29.964
I left the orphans home this morning.

00:22:30.024 --> 00:22:34.296
I want to find a real home with real folks, see?

00:22:34.356 --> 00:22:39.160
It wasn't easy to lose your mother and father, Pollyanna knew.

00:22:39.221 --> 00:22:41.632
So she took Jimmy home.

00:22:41.692 --> 00:22:43.063
And Polly?

00:22:43.123 --> 00:22:44.944
Can Jimmy be and live with us?

00:22:45.004 --> 00:22:46.286
She asked.

00:22:46.346 --> 00:22:49.218
But Aunt Polly said, no.

00:22:49.278 --> 00:22:52.190
And Jimmy left the house sadly.

00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:54.692
Pollyanna ran after him.

00:22:54.752 --> 00:22:56.154
Don't worry.

00:22:56.214 --> 00:23:00.546
I'm going to find you a real home," she told him in the street.

00:23:00.606 --> 00:23:02.526
Maybe the church can help.

00:23:02.586 --> 00:23:04.077
Let's see.

00:23:04.137 --> 00:23:10.489
So Jimmy went back to the orphan's home that night, and Aunt Polly felt bad.

00:23:10.549 --> 00:23:21.540
The next day, she told Nancy, please move Pollyanna's things down from the attic into the bedroom under it.

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:26.608
Chapter four.

00:23:26.668 --> 00:23:29.079
Things go wrong.

00:23:29.139 --> 00:23:35.500
When Nancy told Pollyanna about her new bedroom, she ran at once to her aunt.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:36.961
It's beautiful.

00:23:37.021 --> 00:23:38.131
She cried.

00:23:38.191 --> 00:23:41.112
With its pictures, carpet and curtains.

00:23:41.172 --> 00:23:42.832
Thank you Aunt Polly.

00:23:42.892 --> 00:23:44.463
I'm really glad.

00:23:44.523 --> 00:23:48.384
Pollyanna, please stop being glad about everything.

00:23:48.444 --> 00:23:49.714
I'm tired of it.

00:23:49.774 --> 00:23:51.444
You always say it.

00:23:51.504 --> 00:23:52.454
Why?

00:23:52.514 --> 00:23:54.404
It comes from our game.

00:23:54.464 --> 00:24:05.412
Father, Pollyanna began and then stopped, and Polly didn't like to hear about her father, so she said nothing more about it.

00:24:05.472 --> 00:24:10.496
After dinner that day, Miss Polly phoned the minister's wife.

00:24:10.556 --> 00:24:15.541
I'm sorry, but I can't come to the charity meeting at the church this afternoon.

00:24:15.561 --> 00:24:18.324
I have a bad head.

00:24:18.384 --> 00:24:23.199
When Miss Polly went to her room, Pollyanna went out.

00:24:23.259 --> 00:24:25.651
Good afternoon, ladies.

00:24:25.711 --> 00:24:27.562
I'm Pollyanna Whittier.

00:24:27.622 --> 00:24:33.013
She said when she went into the church meeting, did your aunt send you?

00:24:33.073 --> 00:24:35.063
Asked the minister's wife.

00:24:35.123 --> 00:24:37.584
No, it was my idea.

00:24:37.644 --> 00:24:38.984
Said Pollyanna.

00:24:39.044 --> 00:24:43.374
I want to help Jimmy Bean, a boy from the orphan's home.

00:24:43.434 --> 00:24:48.426
He's ten years old, and he wants real folks and a real home.

00:24:48.486 --> 00:24:51.496
Can one of you ladies take him into your house?

00:24:51.556 --> 00:24:56.638
The ladies talked a lot, but not one wanted to take Jimmy.

00:24:56.698 --> 00:25:00.862
In the end, Pollyanna left the church sadly.

00:25:00.922 --> 00:25:05.936
She didn't go home, but walked far into Pendleton Woods.

00:25:05.996 --> 00:25:09.998
There she found Mr. John Pendleton on the ground.

00:25:10.058 --> 00:25:11.380
What's the matter?

00:25:11.440 --> 00:25:12.640
She asked.

00:25:12.701 --> 00:25:16.413
I fell from those rocks up there and broke my leg.

00:25:16.473 --> 00:25:19.622
He said, I can't move.

00:25:19.682 --> 00:25:23.970
Then he took a key from his coat and gave it to her.

00:25:24.030 --> 00:25:26.042
Here's the key to my house.

00:25:26.102 --> 00:25:28.393
It's not far past those trees.

00:25:28.453 --> 00:25:31.656
Go there, open the front door and go in.

00:25:31.716 --> 00:25:34.998
By the door there's a telephone and a telephone book.

00:25:35.058 --> 00:25:38.880
Find Dr. Thomas Chilton's number and phone him.

00:25:38.940 --> 00:25:42.772
Tell him about my accident near Pendleton Hill Rocks.

00:25:42.832 --> 00:25:46.650
Then wait there for him to arrive and bring him here.

00:25:46.710 --> 00:25:50.798
Pollyanna went off with the key and was soon back.

00:25:50.858 --> 00:25:52.078
Did you get in?

00:25:52.138 --> 00:25:53.960
Mr. Pendleton asked.

00:25:54.020 --> 00:25:55.002
Yes.

00:25:55.062 --> 00:25:56.342
And I phoned.

00:25:56.403 --> 00:25:58.274
And Dr. Chilton's coming.

00:25:58.334 --> 00:26:00.336
But I wanted to stay with you.

00:26:00.396 --> 00:26:04.519
When Dr. Chilton came, he smiled at Pollyanna.

00:26:04.580 --> 00:26:07.582
Thank you, young lady, for your help.

00:26:07.643 --> 00:26:12.375
Then he looked carefully at Mr. Pendleton's leg.

00:26:12.435 --> 00:26:17.218
That evening Pollyanna arrived late for supper.

00:26:17.279 --> 00:26:19.550
Nancy met her at the door.

00:26:19.610 --> 00:26:21.673
Your aunt isn't here.

00:26:21.733 --> 00:26:25.498
She went to Boston suddenly to visit a sick friend.

00:26:25.558 --> 00:26:27.360
And I'm glad.

00:26:27.420 --> 00:26:30.179
Nancy cried Pollyanna.

00:26:30.239 --> 00:26:32.077
It's okay.

00:26:32.138 --> 00:26:34.909
I'm playing the glad game.

00:26:34.969 --> 00:26:36.690
Left Nancy.

00:26:36.750 --> 00:26:44.525
Then Pollyanna told Nancy about John Pendleton's accident and she listened with an open mouth.

00:26:44.585 --> 00:26:50.469
The next day Pollyanna told Jimmy Bean about the ladies' charity meeting.

00:26:50.529 --> 00:26:52.270
I'm sorry.

00:26:52.330 --> 00:26:58.278
She said they were more interested in their charity work in India than in you.

00:26:58.338 --> 00:27:01.255
It's because India's far away, I guess.

00:27:01.315 --> 00:27:03.297
Then she had an idea.

00:27:03.317 --> 00:27:04.938
I know.

00:27:04.958 --> 00:27:10.312
I can write to the ladies from my father's old church out west.

00:27:10.372 --> 00:27:14.646
Maybe they'd like to help you because you're far away.

00:27:14.706 --> 00:27:21.532
Okay, said Jimmy, and he went back to the orphan's home again that night.

00:27:21.592 --> 00:27:28.244
Three days later, after her friend in Boston died, Miss Polly came back home.

00:27:28.304 --> 00:27:32.244
Can I take Mrs. Snow's jelly to someone different today?"

00:27:32.304 --> 00:27:34.716
asked Pollyanna that Thursday.

00:27:34.776 --> 00:27:40.680
He broke his leg, and he needs the jelly more than Mrs. Snow at the moment.

00:27:40.740 --> 00:27:45.794
And Pollyanna told her aunt all about John Pendleton's accident.

00:27:45.855 --> 00:27:50.688
John Pendleton cried Miss Polly, do you know him?

00:27:50.748 --> 00:27:53.270
Yes, said Pollyanna.

00:27:53.330 --> 00:27:56.078
So, can I take him the jelly?

00:27:56.138 --> 00:28:01.066
Very well, said her aunt, but I didn't send you.

00:28:01.126 --> 00:28:04.087
You must be careful not to say that.

00:28:04.148 --> 00:28:09.100
Pollyanna found Dr. Chilton at John Pendleton's house.

00:28:09.160 --> 00:28:10.601
Come in.

00:28:10.661 --> 00:28:15.833
The doctor said, and Pollyanna went into Mr. Pendleton's room.

00:28:15.893 --> 00:28:17.694
Why are you here?

00:28:17.754 --> 00:28:19.835
Cried the man in bed angrily.

00:28:19.855 --> 00:28:22.236
I brought you some jelly.

00:28:22.296 --> 00:28:23.826
Said Pollyanna.

00:28:23.886 --> 00:28:25.316
Nancy made it.

00:28:25.376 --> 00:28:27.346
She works for Aunt Polly.

00:28:27.406 --> 00:28:28.817
And Polly?

00:28:28.877 --> 00:28:30.638
Miss Polly Harrington.

00:28:30.698 --> 00:28:32.028
I lived with her.

00:28:32.088 --> 00:28:33.769
With her?

00:28:33.829 --> 00:28:34.919
He said.

00:28:34.979 --> 00:28:37.520
His face was suddenly white.

00:28:37.580 --> 00:28:38.420
Yes.

00:28:38.481 --> 00:28:40.431
My mother was her sister.

00:28:40.491 --> 00:28:43.712
When father died, they sent me to her.

00:28:43.772 --> 00:28:46.724
Did Miss Polly send that jelly for me?

00:28:46.744 --> 00:28:48.244
Oh no.

00:28:48.304 --> 00:28:50.675
I must be careful not to say that.

00:28:50.735 --> 00:28:51.896
She told me.

00:28:51.956 --> 00:28:53.058
I see.

00:28:53.118 --> 00:28:59.144
said Mr. Pendleton, and he looked at Pollyanna very strangely.

00:28:59.204 --> 00:29:04.399
Dr. Chilton took her home in his buggy soon after that.

00:29:04.459 --> 00:29:12.926
A week after Pollyanna's visit to Mr. Pendleton's house, Ms. Polly went to a lady's charity meeting at the church.

00:29:12.986 --> 00:29:19.380
When she came home, her face was pink and her hair was dark from the rain.

00:29:19.440 --> 00:29:24.190
Why did you go to them about that orphan boy, Pollyanna?

00:29:24.250 --> 00:29:25.781
She asked her niece.

00:29:25.841 --> 00:29:28.212
It was very bad of you.

00:29:28.272 --> 00:29:30.403
Pollyanna didn't listen.

00:29:30.463 --> 00:29:34.846
Your hair is beautiful today, Aunt Polly, she said.

00:29:34.906 --> 00:29:41.098
She took her aunt up to her room, did her hair, and put a red flower in it.

00:29:41.158 --> 00:29:45.017
And Miss Polly couldn't stop her, couldn't punish her.

00:29:45.077 --> 00:29:53.281
Then, suddenly, through the window, they saw Dr. Chilton's buggy in the street with the doctor in it.

00:29:53.341 --> 00:29:57.464
Pollyanna opened the window and called out to him.

00:29:57.524 --> 00:30:00.408
Dr. Chilton, did you want me?

00:30:00.468 --> 00:30:01.848
I'm up here.

00:30:01.908 --> 00:30:05.362
Miss Polly ran from the window at once.

00:30:05.422 --> 00:30:07.013
What's the matter?

00:30:07.073 --> 00:30:09.137
Pollyanna called after her.

00:30:09.197 --> 00:30:11.390
Why did you do that?

00:30:11.450 --> 00:30:16.514
It's not right for folks to see me with a silly flower in my hair!"

00:30:16.574 --> 00:30:20.727
cried her aunt.

00:30:20.787 --> 00:30:33.576
Chapter 5 Someone very important Pollyanna left her aunt upstairs and ran out to Dr. Chilton.

00:30:33.636 --> 00:30:34.816
What is it?

00:30:34.876 --> 00:30:35.942
She asked.

00:30:36.002 --> 00:30:41.582
Mr. Pendleton wants you, so after the rain stopped, I drove over here.

00:30:41.642 --> 00:30:42.942
Can you come?

00:30:43.002 --> 00:30:45.114
I must ask my aunt.

00:30:45.174 --> 00:30:47.697
She came back nearly at once.

00:30:47.757 --> 00:30:48.698
Well?

00:30:48.758 --> 00:30:50.420
asked the doctor.

00:30:50.480 --> 00:30:53.672
I can go, Pollyanna answered.

00:30:53.732 --> 00:30:57.576
But Aunt Polly spoke very strangely to me.

00:30:57.636 --> 00:31:00.598
She said, yes, go.

00:31:00.658 --> 00:31:02.983
Why didn't you leave before?

00:31:03.043 --> 00:31:07.167
Was your aunt upstairs at the window with you when I arrived?

00:31:07.227 --> 00:31:08.768
asked the doctor.

00:31:08.828 --> 00:31:11.438
Yes, did you see her?

00:31:11.498 --> 00:31:13.909
She was beautiful, I thought.

00:31:13.969 --> 00:31:15.650
What did you think?

00:31:15.710 --> 00:31:20.981
The doctor looked at Pollyanna, smiled sadly and said.

00:31:21.041 --> 00:31:26.433
Yes, for me she was beautiful too.

00:31:26.493 --> 00:31:29.274
Oh, I must tell her.

00:31:29.334 --> 00:31:32.074
Pollyanna, please don't.

00:31:32.134 --> 00:31:33.532
Why not?

00:31:33.592 --> 00:31:36.019
It's a nice thing to say.

00:31:36.079 --> 00:31:40.241
But maybe Miss Polly doesn't want to hear it from me.

00:31:40.301 --> 00:31:42.082
Maybe you're right.

00:31:42.142 --> 00:31:45.254
Dr. Warren's her doctor after all.

00:31:45.314 --> 00:31:48.875
And she ran from the window when she saw you here.

00:31:48.936 --> 00:31:53.048
And with that, they went to Mr. Pendleton's house.

00:31:53.108 --> 00:31:56.910
Mr. Pendleton was very happy to see her.

00:31:56.970 --> 00:31:59.241
Do you have more jelly for me?

00:31:59.301 --> 00:32:00.762
Not from Aunt Polly?

00:32:00.822 --> 00:32:02.062
He laughed.

00:32:02.122 --> 00:32:05.373
Pollyanna's face was suddenly red.

00:32:05.433 --> 00:32:08.334
Did I say something wrong on my last visit?

00:32:08.394 --> 00:32:09.614
She asked.

00:32:09.674 --> 00:32:10.555
No.

00:32:10.615 --> 00:32:11.835
He answered.

00:32:11.895 --> 00:32:17.647
He had a box of beautiful old things from China and India by his bed that day.

00:32:17.707 --> 00:32:22.599
They opened it and took them out, and Pollyanna played with them.

00:32:22.659 --> 00:32:25.248
And he and Pollyanna talked.

00:32:25.308 --> 00:32:32.722
They spoke of Nancy, and Polly, and Pollyanna's home with her father and mother out west.

00:32:32.782 --> 00:32:43.760
When it was time for her to go, John Pendleton said quietly, Pollyanna, when I learned about your folks last time, I didn't want to see you again.

00:32:43.820 --> 00:32:50.104
You reminded me of someone once very important for me from years ago, and I felt sad.

00:32:50.164 --> 00:32:54.578
I wanted to forget you, but I can't do without you.

00:32:54.638 --> 00:32:56.219
I know that now.

00:32:56.279 --> 00:32:58.731
So please come and see me often."

00:32:58.790 --> 00:33:03.824
Of course, said Pollyanna.

00:33:03.884 --> 00:33:10.748
After supper, Pollyanna told Nancy about her visit.

00:33:10.808 --> 00:33:13.230
Lots of people don't like him.

00:33:13.290 --> 00:33:16.562
But he's very nice to me, she said.

00:33:16.622 --> 00:33:18.933
And it isn't always easy.

00:33:18.994 --> 00:33:26.966
When I took him the jelly on my last visit, and he heard about my folks, He didn't want to see me again.

00:33:27.026 --> 00:33:28.607
Why's that?

00:33:28.667 --> 00:33:30.509
asked Nancy.

00:33:30.569 --> 00:33:37.996
And Pollyanna told Nancy about the someone very important for Mr Pendleton from years ago.

00:33:38.016 --> 00:33:41.600
That's it, cried Nancy.

00:33:41.660 --> 00:33:43.792
Now I understand.

00:33:43.852 --> 00:33:44.854
What?

00:33:44.914 --> 00:33:46.814
asked Pollyanna.

00:33:46.874 --> 00:34:00.948
Mr. John Pendleton and Miss Polly Harrington were lovers all those years ago, cried Nancy, and she told Pollyanna about old Tom's story.

00:34:01.008 --> 00:34:09.442
But Mr. Pendleton doesn't like Aunt Polly, said Pollyanna, and she didn't want to send him the jelly.

00:34:09.501 --> 00:34:14.615
That's because they quarreled, said Nancy.

00:34:14.675 --> 00:34:23.982
On Pollyanna's next visit to John Pendleton's house, before she left, he again had a quiet talk with her.

00:34:24.042 --> 00:34:27.854
I feel very alone in this big old house, Pollyanna.

00:34:27.914 --> 00:34:33.838
I need a woman's hand and heart, or a child's face, near me to feel at home here.

00:34:33.898 --> 00:34:36.029
Would you like to come and live with me?

00:34:36.089 --> 00:34:37.970
Maybe I can adopt you.

00:34:38.031 --> 00:34:39.541
With Aunt Polly?

00:34:39.601 --> 00:34:40.992
asked Pollyanna.

00:34:41.052 --> 00:34:42.707
Can she come too?

00:34:42.767 --> 00:34:44.221
Aunt Polly?

00:34:44.281 --> 00:34:47.653
Yes, because you loved her all those years ago.

00:34:47.712 --> 00:34:50.543
Well, no, not with Aunt Polly.

00:34:50.603 --> 00:34:52.774
He answered with a red face.

00:34:52.834 --> 00:34:56.245
And please, don't tell people about my plan for now.

00:34:56.305 --> 00:34:57.436
It's a secret.

00:34:57.496 --> 00:34:59.356
Do you understand?

00:34:59.416 --> 00:35:08.879
The next time Dr. Chilton took Pollyanna to Mr. Pendleton's house, she said, I'm going to tell you something, Dr. Chilton.

00:35:08.939 --> 00:35:12.073
It's a secret between Mr. Pendleton and me.

00:35:12.133 --> 00:35:14.858
But I can tell you, I think.

00:35:14.918 --> 00:35:16.900
It's only a secret from her.

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:18.691
Her?

00:35:18.751 --> 00:35:20.572
As Dr. Chilton.

00:35:20.632 --> 00:35:22.114
And Polly.

00:35:22.174 --> 00:35:23.725
Said Pollyanna.

00:35:23.785 --> 00:35:29.890
And she told the doctor all about the old love between Mr. Pendleton and her aunt.

00:35:29.950 --> 00:35:33.462
And about Mr. Pendleton's plans to adopt her.

00:35:33.522 --> 00:35:34.954
Right.

00:35:35.014 --> 00:35:37.236
I didn't know about that.

00:35:37.296 --> 00:35:38.785
Said the doctor.

00:35:38.845 --> 00:35:41.814
And he was quiet for a long time.

00:35:41.874 --> 00:35:45.734
Maybe Mr. Pendleton wants to tell me more about it today.

00:35:45.794 --> 00:35:48.545
Said Pollyanna when they arrived.

00:35:48.605 --> 00:35:49.866
Maybe.

00:35:49.926 --> 00:35:51.526
Said Dr. Chilton.

00:35:51.586 --> 00:35:58.278
And he smiled strangely and drove off in his buggy back to town.

00:35:58.338 --> 00:36:04.089
On that visit, Mr. Pendleton explained everything.

00:36:04.149 --> 00:36:07.270
I didn't love Aunt Polly all those years ago.

00:36:07.330 --> 00:36:09.204
He told Pollyanna.

00:36:09.264 --> 00:36:16.692
I was in love with your mother before she married your father, but she didn't love me back.

00:36:16.712 --> 00:36:20.114
Oh, I see, cried Pollyanna.

00:36:20.174 --> 00:36:23.425
When I met you, you reminded me of her.

00:36:23.485 --> 00:36:26.216
At first I didn't want to see you again.

00:36:26.276 --> 00:36:28.908
But now I want to adopt you.

00:36:28.968 --> 00:36:31.448
And what about Aunt Polly?

00:36:31.508 --> 00:36:34.060
No, I want only you.

00:36:34.120 --> 00:36:36.470
So can you ask her about it?

00:36:36.530 --> 00:36:38.133
All right.

00:36:38.193 --> 00:36:42.340
After her visit, Pollyanna walked back home.

00:36:42.400 --> 00:36:49.777
It began to rain after she left Pendleton Woods, but soon she met Nancy in the street with an umbrella.

00:36:49.838 --> 00:36:55.040
Miss Polly sent me to find you with this," said Nancy.

00:36:55.100 --> 00:36:57.891
She was really worried about you.

00:36:57.951 --> 00:36:59.112
Was she?

00:36:59.172 --> 00:37:00.803
asked Pollyanna.

00:37:00.863 --> 00:37:04.645
She couldn't leave her aunt and live with Mr. Pendleton now.

00:37:04.705 --> 00:37:05.996
She knew that.

00:37:06.056 --> 00:37:10.028
Aunt Polly was worried about her and needed her.

00:37:10.088 --> 00:37:17.704
But Mr. Pendleton really needed a child near him too to make his big old house into a home.

00:37:17.764 --> 00:37:23.056
What could Pollyanna do to make the two of them happy?

00:37:23.116 --> 00:37:26.648
Suddenly, she smiled.

00:37:26.708 --> 00:37:32.509
She had the answer.

00:37:32.570 --> 00:37:48.789
Chapter 6 The Gladest Things On Pollyanna's next visit to John Pendleton's house, he asked Did you speak to your aunt?

00:37:48.849 --> 00:37:50.520
Can you live here?

00:37:50.580 --> 00:37:53.060
No, I can't.

00:37:53.120 --> 00:37:54.850
Did she say no?

00:37:54.910 --> 00:37:57.141
I didn't ask her.

00:37:57.201 --> 00:37:59.051
But she needs me.

00:37:59.111 --> 00:38:02.402
And I have a different child for you to adopt.

00:38:02.462 --> 00:38:04.852
To make your house into a home.

00:38:04.912 --> 00:38:07.133
I'm really glad for him.

00:38:07.193 --> 00:38:08.243
For who?

00:38:08.303 --> 00:38:09.653
Jimmy Bean.

00:38:09.713 --> 00:38:11.424
Cried Pollyanna.

00:38:11.484 --> 00:38:14.902
And she explained about the poor orphan.

00:38:14.962 --> 00:38:19.292
I had a letter from my church ladies out West last week.

00:38:19.352 --> 00:38:22.884
She finished, and nobody wanted him there.

00:38:22.944 --> 00:38:25.065
He was sad about that.

00:38:25.126 --> 00:38:32.440
Pollyanna left with an invitation for Jimmy and her to visit Mr Pendleton next Saturday.

00:38:32.500 --> 00:38:40.454
One Thursday afternoon, Mrs. Snow sent Pollyanna to Dr. Chilton's house for some medicine.

00:38:40.514 --> 00:38:44.523
I never saw your home before, she said.

00:38:44.583 --> 00:38:46.681
There are only rooms.

00:38:46.742 --> 00:38:47.962
He answered.

00:38:48.022 --> 00:38:49.914
Not really a home.

00:38:49.974 --> 00:38:55.448
Do you need the hand and heart of a woman or the face of a child too?

00:38:55.508 --> 00:38:58.110
Mr Pendleton wanted those.

00:38:58.170 --> 00:38:59.872
Said Pollyanna.

00:38:59.932 --> 00:39:00.952
Oh.

00:39:01.012 --> 00:39:05.065
And you remember when I told you about him and Aunt Polly.

00:39:05.126 --> 00:39:07.778
Did you tell any folks that story?

00:39:07.838 --> 00:39:08.869
No.

00:39:08.929 --> 00:39:09.970
Good.

00:39:10.030 --> 00:39:14.351
Because Mr Pendleton explained everything to me later.

00:39:14.411 --> 00:39:18.050
He loved my mother, not Aunt Polly.

00:39:18.110 --> 00:39:21.870
But now he's going to adopt Jimmy Bean.

00:39:21.930 --> 00:39:30.702
So maybe you can get the hand and heart of a woman, or the face of a child, to make your rooms into a home, Dr. Chilton.

00:39:30.762 --> 00:39:34.373
Some women don't give hand and heart very easily.

00:39:34.433 --> 00:39:37.183
He answered quickly and stood up.

00:39:37.243 --> 00:39:39.624
Here's that medicine for Mrs. Snow.

00:39:39.684 --> 00:39:41.026
He said.

00:39:41.086 --> 00:39:47.901
All of this, of course, was before the accident, and that changed everything.

00:39:47.961 --> 00:39:49.882
How did it happen?

00:39:49.942 --> 00:39:54.424
On the last day of October, Pollyanna left school.

00:39:54.484 --> 00:39:59.015
She didn't look to left and right when she walked across the road.

00:39:59.075 --> 00:40:05.190
Suddenly a car hit her, and she fell to the ground unconscious.

00:40:05.250 --> 00:40:08.682
By five o'clock, she was back at home.

00:40:08.743 --> 00:40:12.004
But when would she open her eyes?

00:40:12.064 --> 00:40:18.560
Nancy sat by her bed, and Miss Polly telephoned her doctor at once.

00:40:18.620 --> 00:40:23.413
When Dr. Warren came, he looked at Pollyanna carefully.

00:40:23.474 --> 00:40:29.098
Well, she didn't break an arm or a leg, but she hit her head badly.

00:40:29.158 --> 00:40:30.890
He told Miss Polly.

00:40:30.950 --> 00:40:33.222
And I'm worried.

00:40:33.282 --> 00:40:38.004
Next morning Pollyanna opened her eyes.

00:40:38.064 --> 00:40:39.445
Where am I?

00:40:39.505 --> 00:40:40.986
What happened?

00:40:41.046 --> 00:40:43.228
Why can't I move my legs?

00:40:43.288 --> 00:40:44.818
She cried.

00:40:44.879 --> 00:40:48.910
Miss Polly explained about the accident.

00:40:48.970 --> 00:40:53.454
And now you must sleep, she said.

00:40:53.514 --> 00:41:02.052
So Pollyanna slept for days, and many people from the town came and left flowers for her.

00:41:02.112 --> 00:41:09.998
When John Pendleton arrived soon after Pollyanna's accident, Nancy ran to tell old Tom.

00:41:10.058 --> 00:41:12.290
Mr. Pendleton's here.

00:41:12.350 --> 00:41:14.141
You don't say?

00:41:14.201 --> 00:41:16.212
answered the old man.

00:41:16.272 --> 00:41:20.766
Was he really Miss Polly's lover from long ago?

00:41:20.826 --> 00:41:22.716
asked Nancy.

00:41:22.776 --> 00:41:27.896
I believed that once, but now I'm not sure.

00:41:27.956 --> 00:41:29.768
Don't be silly.

00:41:29.828 --> 00:41:34.360
He loved Miss Jenny, but she loved that young minister.

00:41:34.420 --> 00:41:41.826
When they married and left, Miss Polly felt sorry for John Pendleton and was nice to him.

00:41:41.886 --> 00:41:45.012
Maybe he understood something different.

00:41:45.072 --> 00:41:48.440
But for her, they were only good friends.

00:41:48.500 --> 00:41:54.667
Then, in the town, people began to talk of love between them.

00:41:54.727 --> 00:42:01.664
After that, Miss Polly and John Pendleton quarreled, and he stopped coming here.

00:42:01.725 --> 00:42:07.383
In the front room, Mr. Pendleton asked, How is Pollyanna?

00:42:07.443 --> 00:42:11.717
I don't know, said Miss Polly coldly.

00:42:11.778 --> 00:42:19.251
She can't move her legs, but she talks about when you broke your leg and were in bed for only weeks.

00:42:19.311 --> 00:42:25.404
She's glad because that's different from poor Mrs. Snow in bed for years.

00:42:25.464 --> 00:42:27.054
It's very sad.

00:42:27.114 --> 00:42:28.515
She doesn't understand.

00:42:28.535 --> 00:42:31.786
I wanted Pollyanna to live with me, you know.

00:42:31.846 --> 00:42:41.594
He said, with you, said Miss Polly, Yes, but she wanted to stay here because you needed her, she said.

00:42:41.654 --> 00:42:45.858
Suddenly, tears came to miss Polly's eyes.

00:42:45.918 --> 00:42:51.254
After some weeks, Dr. Warren called a specialist from New York.

00:42:51.314 --> 00:42:55.068
Dr. Mead came and looked at Pollyanna.

00:42:55.128 --> 00:43:00.860
When he left, he spoke quietly to Miss Polly by Pollyanna's door.

00:43:00.920 --> 00:43:07.004
Fluffy the cat was in Pollyanna's room at the time, and she wanted to go out.

00:43:07.064 --> 00:43:14.158
Just then, she pushed the door open, so Pollyanna heard everything.

00:43:14.218 --> 00:43:17.910
Well, she's never going to walk again.

00:43:17.970 --> 00:43:19.762
Said Dr. Mead.

00:43:19.822 --> 00:43:21.734
Poor Pollyanna.

00:43:21.794 --> 00:43:30.662
When she was well, she taught the glad game to Mr. Pendleton, Mrs. Snow, Nancy, and lots of people in town.

00:43:30.722 --> 00:43:34.366
But now, she could never leave her bed.

00:43:34.426 --> 00:43:38.953
It wasn't easy for her to find a thing to be glad about.

00:43:39.014 --> 00:43:44.970
Mr. John Pendleton called on Aunt Polly again when he heard the news.

00:43:45.031 --> 00:43:47.892
Please tell Pollyanna something from me.

00:43:47.952 --> 00:43:50.033
He said before he left.

00:43:50.093 --> 00:43:54.386
Jimmy Bean came to see me, and he's going to be my little boy.

00:43:54.446 --> 00:43:55.976
I'm going to adopt him.

00:43:56.036 --> 00:43:57.207
Tell her that.

00:43:57.267 --> 00:43:59.610
Maybe she can feel glad about it.

00:43:59.670 --> 00:44:05.036
Yes, Mr. Pendleton said Miss Polly in surprise.

00:44:05.096 --> 00:44:10.548
Pollyanna was, of course, very glad to hear the news.

00:44:10.608 --> 00:44:17.922
Back home, Mr. Pendleton and his friend Dr. Chilton sat in the front room and talked.

00:44:17.982 --> 00:44:21.324
You remember your friend at the hospital, Tom?

00:44:21.384 --> 00:44:23.594
Who, the specialist?

00:44:23.654 --> 00:44:27.506
Yes, he helps lots of people to walk after accidents.

00:44:27.566 --> 00:44:29.390
Take Pollyanna to him.

00:44:29.450 --> 00:44:32.087
Maybe he can help her, too.

00:44:32.147 --> 00:44:34.080
I can't, John.

00:44:34.140 --> 00:44:37.496
I must have a look at her before I can call my friend.

00:44:37.556 --> 00:44:40.592
But Dr. Warren is Miss Polly's doctor.

00:44:40.652 --> 00:44:44.014
I can't visit without an invitation from him.

00:44:44.074 --> 00:44:53.727
and after Miss Polly and I quarreled 15 years ago, when folks in town began to call the two of you lovers, she's never going to ask me.

00:44:53.787 --> 00:44:55.148
You know that.

00:44:55.208 --> 00:45:03.833
I'm never going to visit her house again without an invitation from her, and she's never going to change her heart and forgive me.

00:45:03.894 --> 00:45:06.425
Please, Tom, forget all that.

00:45:06.485 --> 00:45:07.926
Think of the girl.

00:45:07.986 --> 00:45:14.652
I'm sorry, John, but without an invitation from Miss Polly, I can't visit Pollyanna.

00:45:14.712 --> 00:45:19.075
Now all this time, the window in the room was open.

00:45:19.135 --> 00:45:25.836
And near the window, because it was Saturday morning, Jimmy Bean was at work in the garden.

00:45:25.897 --> 00:45:31.878
He heard everything, and went at once to speak to Miss Polly.

00:45:31.938 --> 00:45:38.350
That afternoon, an invitation came for Dr. Chilton to visit Pollyanna.

00:45:38.410 --> 00:45:40.336
Did you ask for me?

00:45:40.396 --> 00:45:43.966
Dr. Chilton asked Miss Polly when he arrived.

00:45:44.026 --> 00:45:45.078
I...

00:45:45.138 --> 00:45:47.952
I did, said Miss Polly.

00:45:48.012 --> 00:45:51.076
Her face was suddenly very pink.

00:45:51.136 --> 00:45:58.474
She didn't see Tom Chilton smile happily behind her back when he went up to Polly Anna's room after her.

00:45:58.534 --> 00:46:03.305
When Dr. Chilton left, Miss Polly told Pollyanna.

00:46:03.365 --> 00:46:06.647
Next week, you're going to a hospital.

00:46:06.707 --> 00:46:10.219
A friend of Dr. Chilton's is going to care for you there.

00:46:10.279 --> 00:46:11.870
Maybe he can help you.

00:46:11.930 --> 00:46:13.390
We're going to see.

00:46:13.450 --> 00:46:18.854
And thank you, Pollyanna, for bringing Dr. Chilton back to me.

00:46:18.914 --> 00:46:21.045
I'm very glad.

00:46:21.105 --> 00:46:23.414
Oh, and Polly.

00:46:23.474 --> 00:46:30.328
So you were his woman's hand and heart from long ago, cried Pollyanna happily.

00:46:30.388 --> 00:46:34.911
Some months later, a letter arrived from Pollyanna.

00:46:34.971 --> 00:46:40.074
Mrs. Polly Chilton read it to her husband at breakfast.

00:46:40.134 --> 00:46:47.620
Dear Aunt Polly and Uncle Tom, today I walked from my bed to the window.

00:46:47.640 --> 00:46:50.112
I couldn't believe it.

00:46:50.172 --> 00:46:53.543
At last, I'm starting to walk.

00:46:53.603 --> 00:47:01.138
The doctors watched and smiled when I did it, and the hospital workers had tears in their eyes.

00:47:01.198 --> 00:47:02.828
I didn't cry.

00:47:02.848 --> 00:47:06.061
I wanted to laugh and sing.

00:47:06.121 --> 00:47:07.952
I can walk.

00:47:08.012 --> 00:47:14.206
I arrived here nearly ten months ago, but I'm not worried by that.

00:47:14.266 --> 00:47:17.330
I was there at your wedding after all.

00:47:17.390 --> 00:47:22.563
It was a wonderful idea to have your wedding here by my bed, Aunt Polly.

00:47:22.623 --> 00:47:23.966
Thank you.

00:47:24.026 --> 00:47:27.740
You always think of the Gladest things.

00:47:27.800 --> 00:47:31.181
Soon I can go home, they say.

00:47:31.241 --> 00:47:33.202
I like to walk there.

00:47:33.262 --> 00:47:37.744
I don't want to take a buggy, not when I can go on foot.

00:47:37.804 --> 00:47:42.726
Legs are important, but you don't know it when they're working.

00:47:42.786 --> 00:47:46.418
When I lost my legs, I learned that.

00:47:46.478 --> 00:47:48.969
And I'm very glad about it.

00:47:49.029 --> 00:47:52.156
I'm very glad about everything.

00:47:52.216 --> 00:47:55.877
Tomorrow, I'm going to walk some more.

00:47:55.937 --> 00:47:58.521
Maybe to the door this time.

00:47:58.581 --> 00:48:00.995
Lots of love to everyone.

00:48:01.054 --> 00:48:02.046
Pollyanna.

